{"step_index":220,"source":"SYSTEM","type":"CHECKPOINT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-30T22:02:50Z","content":"# Resuming from a compaction\n\nYou are continuing work on the task described above, but you have lost access to the full conversation history, and need to resume work efficiently using the progress summary below:\n\n# User Requests\nThe following were user requests from the truncated conversation in chronological order:\n1. Build a premium, modern and visually stunning website for a fictional café named \"BREW & BLOOM CAFÉ\" located in Haldia, West Bengal.\r\n\r\nDESIGN:\r\nCreate a sophisticated café brand using warm cream, dark espresso brown, muted sage green and terracotta orange. Use beautiful coffee and food photography, elegant typography, clean layouts, rounded cards and subtle animations. The website must look like a professionally designed real business website, not a generic AI template.\r\n\r\nSECTIONS:\r\n\r\n1. Sticky navigation with logo, Home, Menu, About, Gallery and Contact.\r\n2. Hero section with a stunning café image, headline \"Good Coffee. Slow Moments. Beautiful Days.\", a short description and \"Explore Our Menu\" and \"Order on WhatsApp\" buttons.\r\n3. Featured menu with coffee, tea, cold beverages, pastries and snacks. Display editable sample prices.\r\n4. About section with a short café story and attractive imagery.\r\n5. Photo gallery with a polished responsive grid.\r\n6. Bestsellers section with visually attractive menu \n<truncated 1202 bytes>\n2. Upgrade my existing **Brew & Bloom Café** website into a premium, fully responsive online food ordering and delivery platform. The current website is already working and looks impressive, so preserve its existing structure and features while significantly improving the menu, ordering system, delivery tracking, colour contrast, and animations.\r\n\r\nIMPORTANT: First inspect the existing project, framework, components, and functionality. Modify the existing project instead of creating a new one. Do not remove working features or unnecessarily rewrite the entire application.\r\n\r\n## 1. PREMIUM VISUAL REDESIGN\r\n\r\nMake the website more visually impressive while maintaining a professional café identity.\r\n\r\nUse a sophisticated, high-contrast colour palette:\r\n\r\n* Deep forest green: #073B32\r\n* Dark espresso: #172421\r\n* Vibrant orange: #FF7629\r\n* Golden yellow: #FFC247\r\n* Warm cream: #FFF8EC\r\n* Fresh mint: #D9F3E5\r\n* White: #FFFFFF\r\n* Coral pink and lavender for selected promotional cards.\r\n\r\nUse dark backgrounds for i\n<truncated 11674 bytes>\n3. start\n4.  all good you can continue \n5. Update the existing Brew & Bloom Café website. The website is already working, so do not rebuild it or change its existing design unnecessarily.\r\n\r\n## MAIN REQUIREMENT: WHATSAPP ORDERING\r\n\r\nReplace the current checkout submission flow with a direct WhatsApp ordering system.\r\n\r\nWhen a customer clicks \"Place Order\", \"Order on WhatsApp\", or the final checkout button, redirect them to WhatsApp with a pre-filled message containing their complete order.\r\n\r\n### 1. CONFIGURE THE RESTAURANT WHATSAPP NUMBER\r\n\r\nCreate a single configurable variable for the café owner's WhatsApp number.\r\n\r\nUse a placeholder such as:\r\n919876543210\r\n\r\nThis is an example only. Make it easy for the owner to replace it with their actual WhatsApp number, including the country code, without the + sign, spaces, or dashes.\r\n\r\nDo not invent or assume the real restaurant number.\r\n\r\n### 2. GENERATE THE ORDER MESSAGE AUTOMATICALLY\r\n\r\nRead the customer's actual cart and checkout information and construct a message like this:\r\n\r\nHello Brew & Bloom\n<truncated 3842 bytes>\n\n<summary>\n### 1. Task Overview\n- **Core Request**: Update the existing static website for **Brew & Bloom Café** (located in Haldia, West Bengal) at `C:\\Users\\Lenovo\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\brew-and-bloom\\` to replace the previous checkout submission flow with a direct **WhatsApp Ordering System**.\n- **Success Criteria**:\n  1. Single configurable variable for the restaurant's WhatsApp number (placeholder `919876543210` with country code, no `+`, spaces, or dashes).\n  2. Dynamic generation of order messages matching the exact prompt template (Order ID format `BB-XXXXXX`, items list with quantities and line totals, subtotal, delivery fee, grand total, order type, customer details, landmark if provided, instructions if provided, table/seating if dine-in, payment method, polite closing).\n  3. Proper URL construction (`https://wa.me/919876543210?text=ENCODED_MESSAGE`) with `encodeURIComponent()`.\n  4. Button text updated to `\"Place Order on WhatsApp\"` with the WhatsApp icon, loading state during preparation, accidental repeat click prevention, required field validation (retaining customer on checkout if invalid), and clear error if the WhatsApp number is unconfigured.\n  5. Honest confirmation: explicitly stating opening WhatsApp does NOT mean the order is placed/confirmed; order is confirmed only when the customer sends the message and the café acknowledges it.\n  6. Support for order types: Home Delivery (address required), Takeaway (no address required), and Dine-In (table/seating optional).\n  7. No QR code, no payment gateway, no unnecessary backend. Preserving cart, menu, styling, and animations.\n\n### 2. Progress\n- **Completed**:\n  - `js/config.js`: Defined and exported `export const RESTAURANT_WHATSAPP_NUMBER = '919876543210';` at the top of the file; bound `CONFIG.cafe.whatsapp = RESTAURANT_WHATSAPP_NUMBER`.\n  - `index.html`:\n    - Updated checkout modal form fields: added optional `#custLandmark`, added optional `#custTable` (in `#tableFieldGroup`, hidden unless Dine-In is selected), cleaned payment options to Cash on Delivery and UPI.\n    - Updated main button to `<button type=\"submit\" class=\"btn btn-whatsapp checkout-btn\" id=\"confirmOrderBtn\">` with WhatsApp SVG icon and `<span id=\"confirmOrderBtnText\">Place Order on WhatsApp</span>`.\n    - Added helper note: `\"Your order details will open in WhatsApp. Review your order and press Send to confirm it with the café.\"`\n    - Added honest disclaimer pill: `\"⚠️ Please Note: Opening WhatsApp does not place the order automatically. Your order is confirmed only after you tap Send in WhatsApp and the café acknowledges it with your estimated delivery time.\"`\n    - Added `#whatsappSentDialog` with Order ID display, instructions, \"Re-open WhatsApp\" link, and \"Return to Store\" button.\n  - `script.js`:\n    - Imported `RESTAU